    <task id="LOCAL-00008" summary="fix: enforce SERVING_NOTICE eligibility, close stale-session auth gap, repair KPI/training schema drift&#10;&#10;Auth / session:&#10;- hydrate_request_actor_roles now fails closed (marks the account&#10;  inactive) if the live DB status/role lookup errors, instead of&#10;  silently falling back to the stale JWT claim — closes a gap where a&#10;  transient DB hiccup could let an actor keep acting on a status that&#10;  changed after their token was issued.&#10;- Gate leave_request, wfh, comp_off, optional_leave, and timelog&#10;  routers behind require_onboarding_complete so INVITED/ONBOARDING&#10;  users can't bypass the frontend's OnboardingGate via a direct API call.&#10;&#10;Employment status coverage (ACTIVE-only checks missing SERVING_NOTICE):&#10;- allocation_repository: manager/approver/unallocated-user lookups now&#10;  include SERVING_NOTICE alongside ACTIVE.&#10;- timelog_categories: manager picker includes SERVING_NOTICE.&#10;- scheduled_jobs_service: auto-approver selection includes SERVING_NOTICE.&#10;&#10;Other correctness fixes:&#10;- work_profile: technical-role regex now matches &quot;analyst&quot; roles.&#10;- timelog_service: use format_display_date instead of raw isoformat()&#10;  for CSV/XLSX export and submission messages.&#10;- wk_business_http: map upstream 404s to a clear &quot;not recognized&quot; 404&#10;  instead of a generic 502.&#10;- employee_service: import_user_data and bulk_upload_users now run the&#10;  exit-status/date validation and exit-survey dispatch on status&#10;  changes, matching the single-update path.&#10;&#10;Schema drift repair (guarded migrations for legacy Java-seeded tables):&#10;- Recreate missing training_* enum types when the tables predate this&#10;  app's own migrations.&#10;- Add kpi_definitions.evaluation_criteria, which no migration ever&#10;  actually created despite the model assuming it existed.&#10;- Add B4L/B4H/B5L/B5H bands, mirroring the existing B6L/B6H/B7L/B7H split.&#10;&#10;Also adds app/core/upload_limits.py to raise Starlette's undocumented&#10;1MB multipart part-size cap, wired in on startup.">
